= Reputation system — Simple =

A reputation system summarizes information about what participants did in the past so others can make better decisions about interacting with them. Ratings and reviews are examples. Reputation is evidence, not proof, and the system can be manipulated.

'''Important boundary:''' reputation ≠ identity.

== Sources ==
* Paul Resnick, Richard Zeckhauser, Eric Friedman & Ko Kuwabara, “Reputation Systems” (''Communications of the ACM'', 2000).
* Chrysanthos Dellarocas, “The Digitization of Word of Mouth” (2003).
